{
  "name": "an inverted range",
  "about": "A scale whose lo2 is above its hi2 turns the knob round, and rounds to nearest with ties away from zero.",
  "notes": [
    "out = 100 + round(v * (20 - 100) / 127) = 100 + round(-80 v / 127), ties away from zero.",
    "v 0: 100 = 64.",
    "v 127 (0x7F): 100 - 80 = 20 = 14.",
    "v 64 (0x40): -5120 / 127 = -40.31, rounds to -40, out 60 = 3C.",
    "v 32 (0x20): -2560 / 127 = -20.16, rounds to -20, out 80 = 50.",
    "v 96 (0x60): -7680 / 127 = -60.47, rounds to -60, out 40 = 28.",
    "v 100 (0x64): -8000 / 127 = -62.99, rounds to -63, out 37 = 25. Truncating would give -62 and 38, so this one tells rounding from truncation.",
    "l2 from knob2 scales 0..10 onto 127..0. v 5: 5 * -127 / 10 = -63.5, a NEGATIVE TIE, away from zero is -64, out 63 = 3F. A round half up (JavaScript's Math.round) gives -63 and 64, so this one tells the two tie rules apart.",
    "No cc argument on scale, so it applies to every CC on the link, CC 7 included: v 127 out 14.",
    "NEGATIVE CONTROL: a note's velocity is not a CC value and is not scaled."
  ],
